# Web3Forms access key for the home-page waitlist form.
# Get one free at https://web3forms.com — enter the inbox that should receive
# signups (ailabzsupport@gmail.com) and they email you the key. No account,
# no dashboard: every submission is relayed straight to that inbox.
#
# THE KEY IS THE DESTINATION. Signups go to whichever address the key was
# generated for — nothing in the payload can redirect them, and the address
# shown on the site (CONTACT_EMAIL in Home.jsx) has no effect on delivery.
# Pointing signups at a different inbox means generating a new key, not
# editing code. If mail never arrives, first confirm the key was issued to
# the inbox you're checking: the key itself arrives there by email.
#
# This key is public by design — it only authorises posting to that one form,
# and it ships in the JS bundle like any VITE_ var. It is not a secret.
#
# Leaving it unset makes the form tell visitors to email us instead of
# silently dropping the address, so the site is safe to deploy without it —
# it just won't collect anything.
VITE_WAITLIST_KEY=

# Canonical origin, used at build time for canonical URLs, og:url, absolute
# og:image, sitemap.xml and robots.txt. On Vercel this falls back to the
# project's stable production URL automatically, so it only has to be set once
# a real domain is attached. No trailing slash.
SITE_URL=
